From 37303166a77da08118b9121d44375b1038d240c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NEMO Rung4 executor <executor@nemo.local>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 10:39:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Rung 4: complete symbolic Jacobian pattern + FD oracle;
 production stays analytic

Plumbing only, no physics change. Completes the symbolic Jacobian sparsity
pattern with the live-divisor block and adds the MOSS=0 FD-complete path as a
verification oracle, while production coag-on remains mf=121 (analytic).

Two findings drove the design (both confirmed by the design thread):
- get_jacobian treats rate coefficients as constant, so d(rate)/dY(GRAIN_k) has
  never reached Newton under mf=121; the Rung 3 section 4d claim is retracted (the
  RHS is complete, so gates 3a/3b/3c stand).
- The symbolic pattern was never consumed: MOSS=1 ignores the user IA/JA, so
  numerical == symbolic was byte-identical by construction.

The Rung 4 live divisor (monolayer count SUMLAY) is bounded by construction (its
denominator is floored), so d(SUMLAY)/dY(GRAIN_k) -> 0 as a bin depletes: it is
never the stiff -1/Y^2 reciprocal (that is the dynamic surface-rate GTODN, Rung
5). Completing it is correct plumbing but yields no convergence payoff, and FD is
~4x slower, so production keeps the analytic path; the FD-complete path is kept as
the Rung 5 verification oracle.

Changes:
- global_variables: DECLARED_JAC_{ROW,COL}, NB_DECLARED_JAC_DEPS storage.
- ode_solver: declare_jacobian_dependency (general non-reactant (row,col) facility,
  reused by Rung 5); build_live_divisor_dependencies (GRAIN_RANK-keyed superset
  populator); build_symbolic_sparsity merges declared deps before CSC;
  assert_live_divisor_in_pattern (gate a static completeness check).
- gasgrain: solver_method_flag (production 121; FD-complete 022 via NEMO_ORACLE_MF;
  seam for Rung 5 to retarget coag-on to 021); oracle_mf_override;
  MOSS=0-requires-symbolic guard; gate-a call.
- main: mf from solver_method_flag; DLSODES step-stat accumulation + print (4-IV).
- tests/coag_rung4_sparsity.sh: gate (a) completeness; gate (b) production-vs-oracle
  same-answer + conservation at 20 bins; 4-IV timing.
- docs: as-built outcome (option a, retractions, gate results).

Gates (20-bin fiducial): (a) 12720 live-divisor entries present; (b) 121 vs 022
agree <1% for ab>1e-8, conservation holds, complete pattern byte-inert under 121;
3b/3c pass on production 121 (3b needs its slow-K0 points re-tuned above the 20-bin
noise floor); 4-IV production ~28s vs FD oracle ~118s. Gate (c) retracted (bounded
term). coag-off byte-identical to committed HEAD (equivalence.sh preserved).
